## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model nonstationary, real-world acoustics with online Bayesian tracking and performance under sensor dropouts.

## Key Concepts

- Bayesian online convolutive ICA for time-varying mixing
- Online whitening and fixed-point demixing under nonstationarity
- Handling mic dropouts and strict latency constraints
- Ground-truth SDR/SIR evaluation in dynamic environments

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for online update (high level)
function update(W, X, prior) {
  // whitening
  const Xw = whiten(X);
  // track M(t) via prior
  const M = smoothTrack(W, prior);
  // update demixing
  W = demixUpdate(Xw, M);
  return W;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt the model for moving objects vs. stationary sources?
- What priors best capture rapid, abrupt environmental changes and how would you validate them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical real-time BSS for a CPU-constrained setup with non-stationary noise.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time ICA, frame-based processing, whitening, online demixing, permutation alignment, non-stationary noise tracking
- Trade-offs: time vs frequency domain, learning-rate stability, latency, evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
function onlineDemix(X, W, lr){
  // X: frame batch, W: demixing, lr: learning rate
  const Y = W.map((w,i)=> dot(w, X[i]));
  // simple gradient update placeholder
  const dW = Y.map((y, idx)=> (X[idx] * (sign(y))));
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to combine multi-modal signals with ICA in real time—a practical challenge in modern audio-visual setups used by leading tech companies for conferencing, broadcasting, and assistive listening devices.

## Key Concepts
- Audio-visual fusion for permutation resolution in frequency-domain ICA
- Online ICA with dynamic source count adaptation (2–3 speakers)
- Latency budgets and robustness to video failures
- Feature design for lip cues under variable lighting conditions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: weight update between audio-ICA demixer and video cues
function updateDemixer(audioState, videoState) {
  const wVideo = computeVideoBias(videoState); // robust lip-motion features
  const wAudio = 1 - wVideo;

  const audioUpdate = computeAudioICUpdate(audioState);
  const videoUpdate = computeVideoPermutationBias(videoState);

  return wAudio * audioUpdate + wVideo * videoUpdate;
}

function computeVideoBias(videoState) {
  const lightingCondition = assessLighting(videoState.features);
  const faceDetectionConfidence = videoState.detectionScore;
  return lightingCondition * faceDetectionConfidence;
}
```

